@0    = ~You come. We can finally look each other in the eye, my vessel.~
@1    = ~Who are you?~
@2    = ~What are you?~
@3    = ~Oh great. Another monster. Perhaps we should skip the pleasantries and move right on to the unavoidable fight?~
@4    = ~It is most entertaining that you say this. It truly is proof that we are but one thing.~
@5    = ~I am your blood. I am every drop of this red tincture that's running through your veins; I am what keeps you alive, and bound with who you truly are, <CHARNAME>. I suppose that makes me... you.~
@6    = ~I'm not sure I understand.~
@7    = ~What sort of trick is this?~
@8    = ~I suppose that makes sense. I should have expected that the Bloody Pages of Bhaal would be somehow connected to me.~
@9    = ~It's simple: the book you just touched has connected to your blood. To me. That is what allows us to speak the way we do right now.~
@10   = ~It does make sense, doesn't it? The book has connected to your blood, allowing us to speak the way we do right now.~
@11   = ~I know that you were asked to investigate the book, but truth be told, it works both ways. The book is also studying us, showing us the people that shaped our story. You might have seen Alaundo, Sarevok, and the others—including the man that captured you. Experimented on us; on both you and me.~
@12   = ~The book is like an eye and a mirror. One that allows those like yourself to learn what they need to learn.~
@13   = ~What do I need to learn?~
@14   = ~I don't need to learn anything, or at least not from you. I have no interest in being my father's perfect <PRO_SONDAUGHTER>.~
@15   = ~Many things.~
@16   = ~And do you think you have a choice?~
@17   = ~There are times when you will be given no choice.~
@18   = ~There are times when an obstacle needs to be thrown a couple of floors down.~
@19   = ~What is this? Is this the roof of the Iron Throne headquarters?~
@20   = ~I do know that, and I am not going to hesitate when someone needs to be pushed and taught how to fly.~
@21   = ~I am not going to be like Sarevok!~
@22   = ~Yes. So you remember how we climbed up this tower. Perhaps you also remember how it felt to stand here, look at everything and everyone. Those people were so small. Like ants.~
@23   = ~I never thought that way about them.~
@24   = ~Yes. That's more or less what I thought when I was here.~
@25   = ~I don't think I ever reached the roof. But I must have been on the floor just below us.~
@26   = ~Are you sure? Why wouldn't we have that thought?~
@27   = ~I know. We are the same.~
@28   = ~But you must have at least imagined how it would feel to stand here.~
@29   = ~Good. I'm glad to hear that.~
@30   = ~Aren't we already like your brother?~
@31   = ~There are people who believe reaching towers like this allows people to feel closer to gods. But when we walked the pavement below us, we were just as wonderful. Just as strong. And just as thirsty.~
@32   = ~It's always been like that: the longer one walks, the stronger the thirst becomes. And while we do need to drink water, there is also a different kind of thirst that we suffer from. But you do know that.~
@33   = ~How can you be so sure?~
@34   = ~Yes. I know what you are referring to.~
@35   = ~Because I am your blood. I am your thirst. You do need to feed me, or we both die.~
@36   = ~It sounds like you know what it means to be honest with yourself. And I am quite glad you always knew that it's not just water that we crave.~
@37   = ~Now, will you jump with me? Shall we continue our discussion down there?~
@38   = ~What?! No! Are you insane?~
@39   = ~I don't think this is a good idea.~
@40   = ~Of course. Let us jump. One. Two...~
@41   = ~Have some faith, will you?~
@42   = ~...three.~
@43   = ~Can you feel the thrill that was engraved in this place? This is the place where we killed our brother. This is the place where I rushed through your veins, my vessel! I felt it so strongly. We felt so alive.~
@44   = ~We had to. We had to feel that way. And we had to win. For the sake of everyone that counted on us.~
@45   = ~We had to. We had to feel that way. And we had to win. For the sake of our own survival. It was the key to becoming who we are today.~
@46   = ~I remember that day. I felt powerful. I felt strong. I felt amazing.~
@47   = ~It was always about more than those others you speak of. Do not lie to your own blood!~
@48   = ~Yes. That day made us stronger.~
@49   = ~The book you just touched is your story. And we are the ink. I am the ink.~
@50   = ~Our story is written in blood, <CHARNAME>, and no matter what you do, it's always going to be that way. No matter if you are the first to raise your blade, you will be the last one to hold it.~
@51   = ~Aren't you happy because of it?~
@52   = ~I'm not.~
@53   = ~Of course I am.~
@54   = ~I just want to be left alone.~
@55   = ~I'm doing this because I am given no other choice!~
@56   = ~I'm living the life I was given and... I just got used to it.~
@57   = ~You should learn how to enjoy it more. How to be proud of who we are.~
@58   = ~Yes. Yes, I can feel that pride. It's in me, too.~
@59   = ~Each single day is going to become another page of your story. And the longer you live, the greater the Bloody Pages of Bhaal shall become!~
@60   = ~Continue writing your story. Breathe! Feed me! AND LET ME RUSH THROUGH YOUR VEINS!~